    <http://example.org/activity/activity9> a prov:Activity ;
        prov:startedAtTime "2026-07-10T19:31:18"^^xsd:dateTime ;
        prov:wasAssociatedWith <http://example.org/node/orchestrator> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "1. Context and objectives  Cabinet Vauclair & Associés is a regional accounting and statutory-audit firm (cabinet d’expertise comptable et de commissariat aux comptes) operating several offices across the Belval region, with around 250 staff (chartered accountants, statutory auditors, accounting, payroll and legal collaborators). Cabinet Vauclair & Associés professionals work with a large volume of regulatory and methodological reference material (accounting standards, tax doctrine, the commercial code, collective-bargaining agreements for payroll, internal procedures and methodology guides), under strict confidentiality obligations, and with a strong seasonality of workload (closing periods, tax-return campaigns). As part of a consultation run with a small number of selected vendors, Cabinet Vauclair & Associés wishes to equip The firm’s professionals with an artificial-intelligence assistance solution that improves productivity and the quality and reliability of The firm’s professionals work, while preserving professional secrecy and the reliability of figures — and while remaining strictly a non-decisional support tool.  a consultation run with a small number of selected vendors covers the design, implementation and deployment of such a solution.  2. General description of the need  The solution must provide The firm’s professionals with an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from The firm’s professionals work environment, supporting The firm’s professionals in The firm’s professionals daily activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, supporting them in their daily activities may notably cover:  -   retrieval of regulatory and methodological information; -   assistance in drafting professional documents; -   support in handling client files; -   support for the continuity of missions between collaborators. The solution must fit into existing practices and must not introduce a rupture in Cabinet Vauclair & Associés working methods. The chartered accountant or statutory auditor remains the sole validator: no deliverable is produced or signed without professional validation.  3. Functional scope  3.1 Information consultation assistance. Quick access to reliable, up-to-date information drawn from accounting standards (PCG), tax doctrine and the tax code (CGI), the commercial code and applicable legal texts, collective-bargaining agreements for payroll/social, and Cabinet Vauclair & Associés internal procedures and methodology guides. Answers must be contextualised and grounded in cited sources.  3.2 Drafting assistance. Assistance in drafting client letters and correspondence, mission notes, file memos and syntheses. The solution does not autonomously produce binding or signed deliverables; the professional validates.  3.3 Client-file handling support. During the handling and review of a client file, the solution must surface relevant information, recall applicable rules, propose a checklist of verifications and flag potential anomalies for human review (e.g. during the révision des comptes). the solution must support the preparation of recurring documents. No decision or sign-off may be automated.  3.4 Collaboration and mission continuity. The solution must facilitate the continuity of missions between collaborators by enabling relevant information sharing, an understanding of the context of an in-progress client file, and an efficient resumption by another collaborator.  4. Regulatory, professional and legal constraints  4.1 Professional secrecy and confidentiality. The titleholder must ensure strict respect of professional secrecy and confidentiality of client data. Client files must be strictly partitioned; no leakage of data between client files is acceptable.  4.2 Personal-data protection (GDPR). Client and employee personal and financial data must be processed in compliance with Personal-data protection (GDPR). Data must be hosted within the EU, with no transfer outside the EU; sensitive data must be protected (encryption, pseudonymisation where relevant).  4.3 Reliability and traceability of outputs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding GDPR compliance, our company, Faber IA ISO 27701 certification, which is an extension for privacy information management, ensures that our company, Faber IA have the necessary processes in place to handle personal data in accordance with the regulation. our company, Faber IA also maintain a data processing register and have appointed a Data Protection Officer (DPO), further ensuring our company, Faber IA commitment to GDPR adherence. For hosting, our company, Faber IA partner with OuraneCloud, which holds the SecNumCloud qualification at the hosting layer. partner supports sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU, aligning with the client's requirement for data to be hosted and not transferred outside the EU. our company, Faber IA security controls include secure software development life cycle practices such as code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing by an external provider of equivalent CREST level. our company, Faber IA also have incident response procedures in place, including detection, notification, and remediation, which includes a 72-hour GDPR breach-notification workflow. To address the requirements for complete audit trails and explainability, our company, Faber IA product, Atelier, is designed to provide retrieval trace, audit log, and figure source linking. our product, Atelier, supports internal quality control and statutory audit review, ensuring that outputs are grounded in sources and numeric outputs are not ungrounded. The associated risks primarily revolve around ensuring continuous compliance with evolving regulatory requirements, maintaining the integrity of our company, Faber IA security controls, and mitigating potential breaches or data leaks. However, with our company, Faber IA existing certifications, security measures, and commitment to information security and privacy, our company, Faber IA are well-positioned to manage The associated risks and meet the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance, professional secrecy, auditor independence, separation of duties, anti-money-laundering obligations (LCB-FT), and compliance with legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents. What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with these regulatory requirements? Based on the company context, we is familiar with the contractual expectations of clients bound by professional secrecy. we maintain we regulatory compliance through we Security & Compliance function, specifically monitoring obligations such as GDPR (including Art. 28 processing agreements), professional secrecy, anti-money-laundering framework (LCB-FT), auditor-independence and separation-of-duties rules for statutory audit, legal retention obligations for accounting documents, and emerging EU AI Act requirements. Regarding GDPR compliance, we intellectual property model includes open source components licensed under permissive licenses, and we provide a Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) to the client. Additionally, we ensure that client data ownership is retained by the client, and we reversibility plan provides for the return and deletion of client data at the end of the contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for professional secrecy, auditor independence, separation of duties, and anti-money-laundering obligations, we contractual framework is designed to safeguard professional secrecy, auditor independence, separation of duties, and anti-money-laundering obligations. we are also aware of the importance of complying with legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents. However, we should flag the potential risk of ensuring that we solution does not compromise we professional obligations, particularly with regards to auditor independence and separation of duties. It is essential to carefully review our contractual framework to ensure that our contractual framework respects auditor independence and separation of duties. In terms of compliance, based on the provided context, we appears to be compliant with the mentioned regulatory requirements. Nevertheless, a thorough review of the specific tender requirements and we capabilities would be necessary to confirm we compliance and identify any potential gaps or risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client's budget allocated to the project is €220,000 over 3 years, with an annual operating cost that must remain controlled. Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and what cost-optimisation strategies can our propose to meet The client's budget constraints? our normal deal range and financial capacity indicate that an engagement of €220,000 over 3 years is well within our capabilities. Given the breakdown of costs, with one-off project costs estimated at 40% and recurring run costs at 60%, our can estimate the total cost of the project. The one-off project costs for the first year would be approximately €88,000, which includes framing, design, integration with our production tools, change management, and training." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The recurring run costs over three years would be approximately €132,000, covering platform subscription, hosting/infrastructure, model-inference costs, support, and maintenance. To meet the client's budget constraints and optimize costs, our can propose a cost-efficient configuration such as the sovereign tier with the sovereign European model, which is noted to be the most cost-efficient on the recurring side. propose would help in maintaining a controlled annual operating cost while ensuring our target gross margin of at least 25% and up to 35%. Given these considerations, our projected margin on this contract could be within the range of 25% to 35% of the total contract value, depending on how effectively our can optimize costs without compromising the quality of service. However, without specific details on the exact breakdown of costs associated with each component of the project, the exact breakdown of costs associated with each component of the project remains a general estimation based on our financial context and capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires an intelligent assistance tool that improves productivity, enhances quality and reliability of work, and preserves professional secrecy. What AI components and innovation strategy can we design to meet these requirements, and what are the associated benefits and risks? To meet The client requirements for an intelligent assistance tool, we can leverage we Atelier platform's retrieval-augmented generation capabilities, which provide grounded answers by citing relevant passages from a controlled corpus. leverage ensures that the generated content is reliable, accurate, and trustworthy. we hybrid retrieval approach, combining lexical and semantic search, enables efficient and effective information retrieval. The re-ranking and query reformulation capabilities further enhance the accuracy of the retrieved information. By leveraging The re-ranking and query reformulation capabilities, we can design an intelligent assistance tool that provides professionals with quick access to relevant and reliable information, thus improving productivity and enhancing the quality and reliability of professionals work. The template-guided drafting capability can assist professionals in generating client letters, mission notes, and file syntheses, which will help preserve professional secrecy by ensuring that sensitive information is handled correctly and securely." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we explainability features, including source citations, retrieved passages, and retrieval traces, provide transparency and accountability, allowing professionals to validate the generated content. we iterative approach to methodologies, involving corpus curation, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design, and evaluation loops, ensures that the solution is tailored to the client's specific needs and requirements. Our iterative approach to methodologies, involving corpus curation, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design, and evaluation loops also allows for continuous improvement and adaptation to changing requirements. The benefits of Our iterative approach to methodologies, involving corpus curation, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design, and evaluation loops include improved productivity, enhanced quality and reliability of work, and preservation of professional secrecy. The associated risks are mitigated by we commitment to explainability, transparency, and accountability, as well as we adherence to The client constraints and requirements. In terms of innovation strategy, we can adopt a progressive deployment approach, starting with a pilot phase to test and refine the solution before scaling up to the entire organization. adopt will enable we to address any potential issues or concerns in a controlled environment and ensure a smooth transition to the new intelligent assistance tool. By leveraging our Atelier platform's capabilities and following an iterative and adaptive approach, we can design an intelligent assistance tool that meets the client's requirements and provides significant benefits while minimizing risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the solution and rely on low-carbon infrastructure. What CSR and sustainability measures can we implement to meet wishes, and how will we report on we environmental performance? At we, we have already conducted a bilan carbone and have a published trajectory to reduce we carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year. we also report the deployment footprint to clients. In terms of infrastructure, we partner with green hosting providers such as OuraneCloud in the EU, which uses renewable energy, has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, and reuses heat." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we digital sobriety practices include model right-sizing, caching, and batching to optimize energy efficiency. we also have carbon reporting capability, which will enable we to track and report on we environmental performance. Furthermore, we inference efficiency is used as an energy lever, ensuring that we operations are environmentally sustainable. By leveraging these capabilities, we can meet the client's requirement for low-carbon infrastructure and provide regular reporting on we environmental performance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA proposes an artificial-intelligence assistance solution designed to improve productivity and the quality and reliability of work for Cabinet Vauclair & Associés' professionals. Faber IA hybrid delivery model combines agile iterations with a phase-gate structure, ensuring a structured and flexible approach to managing the project. The phases include Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run, each ending with a formal review and a go/no-go decision. Faber IA flagship product, Atelier, is a sovereign platform that forges document-grounded AI assistants from an organization's own documents. forges will enable Faber IA to deliver a solution that fits into existing practices and provides quick access to reliable information. Faber IA will utilize Faber IA retrieval-augmented generation capabilities, which provide grounded answers by citing relevant passages from a controlled corpus, ensuring that the generated content is reliable, accurate, and trustworthy. The solution will support Faber IA professionals in the firm's professionals daily activities, including retrieval of regulatory and methodological information, assistance in drafting professional documents, support in handling client files, and collaboration and mission continuity. Faber IA template-guided drafting capability will assist professionals in generating client letters, mission notes, and file syntheses, preserving professional secrecy by ensuring that sensitive information is handled correctly and securely. Faber IA will ensure that the chartered accountant or statutory auditor remains the sole validator of deliverables and that The solution maintains internal quality control, supports statutory-audit review, and complies with anti-money-laundering obligations. The solution will also preserve professional secrecy and ensure continuity of missions between collaborators. In terms of technical constraints, Faber IA will deploy The solution on the sovereign tier of OuraneCloud, utilizing the European open-weight model to ensure compliance with the requirement for no dependency on non-European suppliers. This setup provides the necessary high availability, appropriate response times, and integration capabilities as required. Faber IA API-first approach will satisfy the API-type interface requirement, while Faber IA support for SSO protocols will ensure seamless integration with the client's user directory. For security and compliance, Faber IA have achieved ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the scope of development, delivery, and operations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Any figure or factual statement produced by The solution must be grounded in, and traceable to, a source document; no ungrounded numeric output is acceptable. A complete audit trail and explainability are required, to support Cabinet Vauclair & Associés internal quality control and statutory-audit review.  4.4 Professional responsibility and independence. The solution is a non-decisional assistance tool; the chartered accountant or statutory auditor validates and signs. For statutory-audit (CAC) missions, The solution must respect the auditor’s independence and the separation of duties. The solution must not undermine Cabinet Vauclair & Associés anti-money-laundering obligations (LCB-FT). The titleholder must comply with the legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents.  5. Technical constraints  5.1 Performance. Response times compatible with daily professional use are expected — as an indication, below 2 seconds for common queries — and The solution must sustain The solution performance during seasonal peak loads (closing periods, tax campaigns).  5.2 Availability. A high level of availability during business hours is required, with resilience to seasonal peak loads.  5.3 Integration and interoperability. The solution must integrate with Cabinet Vauclair & Associés production tools (accounting-production software, payroll software, document management / GED) and with the electronic-invoicing / dematerialisation environment. API-type interfaces are expected, as is integration with the user directory (SSO).  6. Sovereignty constraints  Given the confidential financial nature of the data, hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent is preferred, and particular attention will be paid to dependency on non-European suppliers.  7. Budget constraints  The budget allocated to the project is, as an indication, €220,000 over 3 years. The annual operating cost must remain controlled. As Cabinet Vauclair & Associés is an SME, the titleholder must propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service.  8. Environmental constraints  Cabinet Vauclair & Associés wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the solution and to rely, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure.  9. Deployment terms  the project must be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on one office or one mission line, followed by progressive generalisation. Change-management support and training are expected. Ideally, a pilot should be operational before the next closing / tax campaign.  10. Evaluation criteria  Offers will be evaluated against: quality and relevance of the solution; reliability and traceability of outputs; confidentiality and security; respect of professional secrecy and of auditor independence; data sovereignty; quality of integration with Cabinet Vauclair & Associés production tools; total cost; quality of support; environmental considerations; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA use encryption in transit via TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, and Faber IA key management is based on EU-based infrastructure. Faber IA also implement strict partitioning of client files with logical isolation per client and per mission, along with access controls to prevent any cross-client circulation of data. The solution is designed to provide complete audit trails and explainability, supporting internal quality control and statutory audit review. Faber IA will ensure that outputs are grounded in sources and numeric outputs are not ungrounded. Faber IA incident response procedures include detection, notification, and remediation, which includes a 72-hour GDPR breach-notification workflow. In terms of budget, Faber IA estimated total cost for the project is €220,000 over 3 years, with one-off project costs estimated at 40% and recurring run costs at 60%. Faber IA can propose a cost-efficient configuration such as the sovereign tier with the sovereign European model, which is noted to be the most cost-efficient on the recurring side. a cost-efficient configuration such as the sovereign tier with the sovereign European model, which is noted to be the most cost-efficient on the recurring side will help in maintaining a controlled annual operating cost while ensuring Faber IA target gross margin of at least 25% and up to 35%. Faber IA are committed to environmental sustainability and have already conducted a bilan carbone and have a published trajectory to reduce Faber IA carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year. Faber IA partner with green hosting providers such as OuraneCloud in the EU, which uses renewable energy, has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, and reuses heat. Faber IA digital sobriety practices include model right-sizing, caching, and batching to optimize energy efficiency. Faber IA propose a progressive deployment approach, starting with a pilot phase to test and refine the solution before scaling up to the entire organization. a progressive deployment approach will enable Faber IA to address any potential issues or concerns in a controlled environment and ensure a smooth transition to the new intelligent assistance tool. Faber IA joint steering committee and operational committee, with a single accountable project director as the point of contact, will ensure that all requirements are met and that the project is delivered successfully." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "1. Context and objectives  Cabinet Vauclair & Associés is a regional accounting and statutory-audit firm (cabinet d’expertise comptable et de commissariat aux comptes) operating several offices across the Belval region, with around 250 staff (chartered accountants, statutory auditors, accounting, payroll and legal collaborators). Cabinet Vauclair & Associés professionals work with a large volume of regulatory and methodological reference material (accounting standards, tax doctrine, the commercial code, collective-bargaining agreements for payroll, internal procedures and methodology guides), under strict confidentiality obligations, and with a strong seasonality of workload (closing periods, tax-return campaigns). As part of a consultation run with a small number of selected vendors, Cabinet Vauclair & Associés wishes to equip The firm’s professionals with an artificial-intelligence assistance solution that improves productivity and the quality and reliability of The firm’s professionals work, while preserving professional secrecy and the reliability of figures — and while remaining strictly a non-decisional support tool.  a consultation run with a small number of selected vendors covers the design, implementation and deployment of such a solution.  2. General description of the need  The solution must provide The firm’s professionals with an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from The firm’s professionals work environment, supporting The firm’s professionals in The firm’s professionals daily activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, supporting them in their daily activities may notably cover:  -   retrieval of regulatory and methodological information; -   assistance in drafting professional documents; -   support in handling client files; -   support for the continuity of missions between collaborators. The solution must fit into existing practices and must not introduce a rupture in Cabinet Vauclair & Associés working methods. The chartered accountant or statutory auditor remains the sole validator: no deliverable is produced or signed without professional validation.  3. Functional scope  3.1 Information consultation assistance. Quick access to reliable, up-to-date information drawn from accounting standards (PCG), tax doctrine and the tax code (CGI), the commercial code and applicable legal texts, collective-bargaining agreements for payroll/social, and Cabinet Vauclair & Associés internal procedures and methodology guides. Answers must be contextualised and grounded in cited sources.  3.2 Drafting assistance. Assistance in drafting client letters and correspondence, mission notes, file memos and syntheses. The solution does not autonomously produce binding or signed deliverables; the professional validates.  3.3 Client-file handling support. During the handling and review of a client file, the solution must surface relevant information, recall applicable rules, propose a checklist of verifications and flag potential anomalies for human review (e.g. during the révision des comptes). the solution must support the preparation of recurring documents. No decision or sign-off may be automated.  3.4 Collaboration and mission continuity. The solution must facilitate the continuity of missions between collaborators by enabling relevant information sharing, an understanding of the context of an in-progress client file, and an efficient resumption by another collaborator.  4. Regulatory, professional and legal constraints  4.1 Professional secrecy and confidentiality. The titleholder must ensure strict respect of professional secrecy and confidentiality of client data. Client files must be strictly partitioned; no leakage of data between client files is acceptable.  4.2 Personal-data protection (GDPR). Client and employee personal and financial data must be processed in compliance with Personal-data protection (GDPR). Data must be hosted within the EU, with no transfer outside the EU; sensitive data must be protected (encryption, pseudonymisation where relevant).  4.3 Reliability and traceability of outputs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Any figure or factual statement produced by The solution must be grounded in, and traceable to, a source document; no ungrounded numeric output is acceptable. A complete audit trail and explainability are required, to support Cabinet Vauclair & Associés internal quality control and statutory-audit review.  4.4 Professional responsibility and independence. The solution is a non-decisional assistance tool; the chartered accountant or statutory auditor validates and signs. For statutory-audit (CAC) missions, The solution must respect the auditor’s independence and the separation of duties. The solution must not undermine Cabinet Vauclair & Associés anti-money-laundering obligations (LCB-FT). The titleholder must comply with the legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents.  5. Technical constraints  5.1 Performance. Response times compatible with daily professional use are expected — as an indication, below 2 seconds for common queries — and The solution must sustain The solution performance during seasonal peak loads (closing periods, tax campaigns).  5.2 Availability. A high level of availability during business hours is required, with resilience to seasonal peak loads.  5.3 Integration and interoperability. The solution must integrate with Cabinet Vauclair & Associés production tools (accounting-production software, payroll software, document management / GED) and with the electronic-invoicing / dematerialisation environment. API-type interfaces are expected, as is integration with the user directory (SSO).  6. Sovereignty constraints  Given the confidential financial nature of the data, hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent is preferred, and particular attention will be paid to dependency on non-European suppliers.  7. Budget constraints  The budget allocated to the project is, as an indication, €220,000 over 3 years. The annual operating cost must remain controlled. As Cabinet Vauclair & Associés is an SME, the titleholder must propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service.  8. Environmental constraints  Cabinet Vauclair & Associés wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the solution and to rely, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure.  9. Deployment terms  the project must be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on one office or one mission line, followed by progressive generalisation. Change-management support and training are expected. Ideally, a pilot should be operational before the next closing / tax campaign.  10. Evaluation criteria  Offers will be evaluated against: quality and relevance of the solution; reliability and traceability of outputs; confidentiality and security; respect of professional secrecy and of auditor independence; data sovereignty; quality of integration with Cabinet Vauclair & Associés production tools; total cost; quality of support; environmental considerations; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the requirements to improve productivity, enhance quality and reliability of work, preserve professional secrecy, access regulatory and methodological information, receive assistance in drafting professional documents, obtain support in handling client files, ensure continuity of missions between collaborators, provide an intelligent assistance tool, fit into existing practices, remain the sole validator for deliverables, maintain internal quality control, support statutory-audit review, comply with anti-money-laundering obligations, and ensure professional secrecy, what is our project management approach to meet these requirements, and how will our ensure a coherent tender response? Our company, Faber IA, will employ a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure to manage the project. a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure will enable our to address the client's requirements in a structured and flexible manner. The phases of our project management methodology include Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run, each ending with a formal review and a go/no-go decision. During Framing, our will pay particular attention to confidentiality, existing production tools, and seasonality of workload, which is crucial for professional services clients. our dedicated team, consisting of a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, security compliance lead, and additional resources for change management and training, will work closely with the client to ensure that all requirements are met." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To provide an intelligent assistance tool, our will utilize our flagship product, Atelier, which is a sovereign platform that forges document-grounded AI assistants from an organization's own documents. utilize will enable our to deliver a solution that fits into existing practices and provides quick access to reliable information. our will ensure that the chartered accountant or statutory auditor remains the sole validator of deliverables and that our solution maintains internal quality control, supports statutory-audit review, and complies with anti-money-laundering obligations. our solution will also preserve professional secrecy and ensure continuity of missions between collaborators. To guarantee a coherent tender response, our will establish a joint steering committee and operational committee, with a single accountable project director as the point of contact. Roles will be formalized in a RACI matrix, and an escalation path will be documented to address any issues that may arise during the project. By leveraging our expertise, existing partnerships, such as with OuraneCloud for hosting and Ligeo Conseil for integration, and our experience in delivering similar projects, our are confident that our can meet the client's requirements and provide a successful solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires response times below 2 seconds for common queries, high availability during business hours, integration with production tools, API-type interfaces, integration with the user directory (SSO), hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, and no dependency on non-European suppliers. For each requirement, state whether each requirement is FULLY COVERED, PARTIALLY COVERED, or NOT COVERED by our current stack, and describe the proposed architecture to meet these technical constraints. The client requirements can be addressed as follows:  Response times below 2 seconds for common queries are PARTIALLY COVERED because our platform's median latency is 1.3 seconds and the p95 latency is below 2.5 seconds, which suggests that while many queries will meet this requirement, there might be some exceptions. High availability during business hours is FULLY COVERED as our platform's offers high availability during business hours and resilience to peak loads on the appropriate hosting tier. Integration with production tools is PARTIALLY COVERED since our have connectors and adapters for various business tools including accounting-production and payroll software, but it's not explicitly stated that connectors and adapters for various business tools including accounting-production and payroll software cover all the client's production tools. API-type interfaces are FULLY COVERED because our architecture is API-first, using REST and webhooks, which matches the requirement for API-type interfaces. Integration with the user directory (SSO) is FULLY COVERED as our support SSO through SAML and OIDC, along with integration with user directories like LDAP and Entra ID." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent is PARTIALLY COVERED because our sovereign tier hosting option is provided by OuraneCloud, which is described as SecNumCloud-qualified, EU-only, and renewable-powered. However, it's not explicitly stated that our sovereign tier hosting option meets all the client's specific security requirements. No dependency on non-European suppliers is FULLY COVERED for our sovereign European open-weight model hosted by Faber IA on OuraneCloud, which is described as SecNumCloud-qualified, EU-only, and renewable-powered, ensuring full sovereignty and no reliance on non-European providers. The proposed architecture to meet these technical constraints would involve deploying our Atelier platform on the sovereign tier of OuraneCloud, which is described as SecNumCloud-qualified, EU-only, and renewable-powered, utilizing the European open-weight model to ensure compliance with the requirement for no dependency on non-European suppliers. deploying provides the necessary high availability, appropriate response times, and integration capabilities as required. Additionally, implementing our API-first approach will satisfy the API-type interface requirement, while our support for SSO protocols will ensure seamless integration with the client's user directory. To fully meet the production tool integration requirement, further assessment and potential customization of our connectors and adapters may be necessary." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires strict respect of professional secrecy and confidentiality of client data, compliance with GDPR, hosting within the EU, no transfer outside the EU, protection of sensitive data using encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant, a complete audit trail, and explainability. What security measures do we need to implement to ensure compliance with these requirements, and what are the associated risks? To address the client's requirements, our company, Faber IA, already implements several security measures that align with the client's needs. our company, Faber IA have achieved ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the scope of development, delivery, and operations. ISO 27001 certification demonstrates our company, Faber IA commitment to information security management. For data protection, our company, Faber IA use encryption in transit via TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256. our company, Faber IA key management is based on the EU-based infrastructure, ensuring that sensitive data is protected. our company, Faber IA also implement strict partitioning of client files with logical isolation per client and per mission, along with access controls to prevent any cross-client circulation of data. Additionally, our company, Faber IA use pseudonymisation where relevant." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

